  "generated_model": "Let $M = \\{1,2,3\\}$ be the set of workstations, and $N = \\{1,2,\\ldots,101\\}$ the set of radio models, with model $k$ denoted as HiFi$k$.\n\nLet $x_k \\in \\mathbb{Z}_+, \\; k=1,\\ldots,101$ be the number of units of HiFi$k$ produced per day (integer, $\\geq 0$).\n\nLet $t_{mk}$ be the processing time (in minutes) required at workstation $m$ for one unit of HiFi$k$ (from the data below).\n\nLet $C_m$ be the effective daily capacity (in minutes) of workstation $m$ after maintenance.\n\nDefine the idle time at workstation $m$ as $I_m = C_m - \\sum_{k=1}^{101} t_{mk} x_k$.\n\nObjective:\n\\[\n\\min \\sum_{m=1}^3 I_m = \\sum_{m=1}^3 \\left[ C_m - \\sum_{k=1}^{101} t_{mk} x_k \\right]\n\\]\nwhich is equivalent to\n\\[\n\\max \\sum_{m=1}^3 \\sum_{k=1}^{101} t_{mk} x_k\n\\]\nsubject to the constraints below.\n\nConstraints:\n\\[\n\\sum_{k=1}^{101} t_{mk} x_k \\leq C_m \\qquad \\forall m=1,2,3\n\\]\n\\[\nx_k \\in \\mathbb{Z}_+, \\qquad \\forall k=1,\\ldots,101\n\\]\n\nParameters (from retrieved data):\n\n- Total daily time per workstation: $T = 1440$ minutes.\n- Maintenance percentages:\n  - Workstation 1: $10\\%$ ($C_1 = 1440 \\times 0.90 = 1296$)\n  - Workstation 2: $14\\%$ ($C_2 = 1440 \\times 0.86 = 1238.4$)\n  - Workstation 3: $12\\%$ ($C_3 = 1440 \\times 0.88 = 1267.2$)\n\n- Processing times $t_{mk}$ (minutes per unit):\n\nWorkstation 1 (maintenance percent: 10):\n| Model      | Minutes | Model      | Minutes | ... | Model      | Minutes |\n|------------|---------|------------|---------|-----|------------|---------|\n| HiFi1      | 6       | HiFi2      | 4       | ... | HiFi101    | 9       |\n\nWorkstation 2 (maintenance percent: 14):\n| Model      | Minutes | Model      | Minutes | ... | Model      | Minutes |\n|------------|---------|------------|---------|-----|------------|---------|\n| HiFi1      | 5       | HiFi2      | 5       | ... | HiFi101    | 3       |\n\nWorkstation 3 (maintenance percent: 12):\n| Model      | Minutes | Model   